From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew Youll <adyoull@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 22:56:03 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] RISC OS: output to a log file, heap in a dynamic area

- A desktop program must not print (text would appear over the
  desktop): stdout and stderr go to the file named by fheroes2$Log, or
  nowhere when it isn't set. RISC OS allows only one open for writing,
  so the file is opened once for stderr and stdout shares the handle.
- The C heap goes in the dynamic area "fheroes2 Heap" (UnixLib), so
  the WimpSlot only needs to hold the program.
---
 src/engine/riscos.cpp          | 60 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/engine/riscos.h            | 31 ++++++++++++++++++
 src/fheroes2/game/fheroes2.cpp |  7 ++++
 3 files changed, 98 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 src/engine/riscos.cpp
 create mode 100644 src/engine/riscos.h

diff --git a/src/engine/riscos.cpp b/src/engine/riscos.cpp
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..bf05b1c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/engine/riscos.cpp
@@ -0,0 +1,60 @@
